---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import ScrollReveal from "../components/ScrollReveal.tsx";
import { SITE } from "../config/site.mjs";
---

<Layout
  title={`About | ${SITE.title}`}
  description="Giveth House is the physical home of the Giveth Galaxy, a community home in Barcelona open to builders, contributors, and communities since 2017."
  canonicalURL={`${SITE.url}/about`}
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" role="main">
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 md:py-20">
      <ScrollReveal client:idle>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-ink mb-4">Giveth House</h1>
      </ScrollReveal>
      <ScrollReveal client:load delay={0.1}>
        <p class="text-xl text-ink-muted mb-12">
          A home in Barcelona where Web3 builders and communities can live, work and try
          things together.
        </p>
      </ScrollReveal>

      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">

        <ScrollReveal client:load delay={0.2}>
          <h2>Story</h2>
          <p>
            Giveth was founded in 2016 by altruists from the early Ethereum ecosystem. Their
            mission was to build open, decentralized infrastructure to fund public goods and
            reward people who give to society. A year later, Giveth House opened in Barcelona,
            a base in real life for a community spread across the world.
          </p>
          <p>
            The house started with a practical problem. In 2017 the Giveth team held a retreat
            in Berlin, and renting the space cost $5,000–6,000 for the week.{" "}
            <strong>Griff Green</strong> did the math: in Barcelona, that same money could
            rent a house for four months. What began as a way to save on logistics became a
            permanent base for a decentralised community that had no fixed address.
          </p>
          <p>
            The first house was near the Sagrada Família, and the neighbours assumed it was an
            illegal Airbnb. The team later moved to Sants, a working-class neighbourhood with
            a cooperative culture that fit better with what the house wanted to be. It has been
            there ever since.
          </p>
          <p>
            Nine years later, the house is a meeting point for contributors across the
            decentralised ecosystem. People arrive for a conference, a collaboration or a few
            weeks of focused work, and often leave with new friends and new projects.
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>

        <ScrollReveal client:load delay={0.3}>
          <h2>Why Barcelona</h2>
          <p>
            Barcelona was a deliberate choice. Giveth's founders had seen the Catalan struggle
            for independence up close, and wanted a place that stands for freedom of thought
            and freedom of choice, where those freedoms are practiced in real life.
          </p>
          <p>
            Giveth House welcomes people from all walks of life who share a belief in equality,
            safety, camaraderie and freedom from hierarchy. Sants, with its long history of
            workers' movements and cooperative culture, felt like a natural home for a
            solarpunk, blockchain4good community.
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>

        <ScrollReveal client:load delay={0.4}>
          <h2>Community</h2>
          <p>
            Giveth House is the physical home of the Giveth Galaxy, a growing community of
            connected projects and DAOs who care about the common good. Over the years the
            house has welcomed people from Ethereum Foundation, Arbitrum, Starknet, Dappnode,
            Fuel Labs, dOrg, Vocdoni, Talent Layer, General Magic and many others. Some stay a
            few days, others a few weeks. What they share is curiosity about building new ways
            to coordinate and cooperate.
          </p>
          <p>
            It is more than a place to sleep. The house is a{" "}
            <strong>Schelling point for the Web3 ecosystem</strong>: somewhere people naturally
            end up meeting, and where collaborations, friendships and new ideas start on their
            own.
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>

        <ScrollReveal client:load delay={0.5}>
          <h2>Values</h2>
          <p>
            Giveth House is a human place, not a polished coworking space or a startup office.
            It is shaped by:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>openness and freedom of thought</li>
            <li>cooperation and camaraderie</li>
            <li>regenerative economics and public goods</li>
            <li>solarpunk optimism: building better systems together</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Many people call the house <strong>solarpunk</strong>: optimistic and
            collaborative. It is a place where the values behind the code become real.
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>

        <ScrollReveal client:load delay={0.6}>
          <h2>Stewardship</h2>
          <p>
            Since 2022, <strong>Franco Ruiz</strong> has looked after the house. He coordinates
            guest stays, maintains the space, organizes activities and helps residents and
            visitors work together.
          </p>
          <p>
            The house has grown over the years. The latest addition is a third floor with a
            rooftop terrace, an open space the community had long dreamed of, to gather and
            enjoy Barcelona. In 2024, the neighbourhood demolition that had threatened the house
            was officially cancelled. Giveth House is here to stay.
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>

        <ScrollReveal client:load delay={0.7}>
          <h2>Support the House</h2>
          <p>
            Giveth House exists because the community chooses to support it. Donations from
            people across the ecosystem pay for the practical things that keep a shared house
            going: rent, utilities, maintenance and day-to-day costs.
          </p>
          <p>
            The aim is for the house to stay a free, open resource for the Web3 ecosystem, where
            the next generation of builders finds community and a warm welcome in Barcelona.
            Every contribution helps keep it going.
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
